message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Survival of the Fitted: Cross-Checkpoint Transfer of a Jacobian Lens from Qwen3.6-27B to Qwen3.8-27B"
abstract: >-
  A Jacobian lens fitted on Qwen3.6-27B is applied without refitting to
  Qwen3.8-27B and evaluated on latent-entity recovery in two-hop prompts,
  teacher-forced next-token rank on WikiText-103, and a lens-derived
  direction ablation. The latent-entity readout survives the version change
  with a depth-dependent cost; the next-token readout shows a lens-specific
  cost concentrated near layer 48; the ablation removes the target word from
  generation on both checkpoints. The lens remains informative across a
  nearby, architecture-compatible version change without preserving its
  original calibration.
